  "turns": [
    {
      "_id": "0",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "A rectangle has a perimeter of 36 centimeters, and its length is twice its width — we need the area.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t001",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:00:00.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:00:37.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "1",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 2,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So we know the perimeter is 36, and length equals two times width, and we're solving for area.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t002",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:00:41.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:01:47.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "2",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 3,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's the problem in full — nothing more given, so let's get into it.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t003",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:01:52.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:02:33.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "3",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 4,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Okay, let's start plugging what we know into the perimeter formula.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t004",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:02:34.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:03:39.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "4",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 5,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go ahead, write out the perimeter formula with the given values.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t005",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:03:47.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:04:44.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "5",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 6,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Perimeter equals 2 times (length plus width), so that's 2(length + width) = 36.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t006",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:04:51.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:05:36.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "6",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 7,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good, that's the basic setup written down.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t007",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:05:36.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:05:49.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "7",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 8,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Let me think about how to express length and width using just one variable.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t008",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:05:49.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:06:12.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "8",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 9,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go on, how would you set that up?",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t009",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:06:20.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:07:15.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "9",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 10,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Let's call the width w, so since length is twice the width, length is 2w.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t010",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:07:23.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:07:49.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "10",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 11,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, so 2(length + width) becomes 2(2w + w).",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t011",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:07:57.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:08:23.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "11",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 12,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "That simplifies to 2 times 3w, which is 6w.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t012",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:08:24.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:09:21.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "12",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 13,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "So the perimeter equation becomes 6w = 36.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t013",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:09:28.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:10:18.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "13",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 14,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "That's just one equation with one unknown now, so it should be simple to solve.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t014",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:10:25.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:11:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "14",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 15,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good, the equation is set up — nothing solved yet.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t015",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:11:21.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:12:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "15",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 16,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Let's solve 6w = 36 for the width first.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t016",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:12:22.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:13:21.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "16",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 17,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go ahead, solve for w and then find the length and area.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t017",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:13:22.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:13:55.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "17",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 18,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "w = 6, so the width is 6 cm, the length is 12 cm, and the area is 6 times 12, which is 72.",
      "turn_id": "demo-c-s01-t018",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:13:55.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:14:07.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "18",
      "session_id": "demo-c-s01",
      "sequence_id": 19,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Great, that gives us an area of 72 square centimeters.",
